<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Nov 27.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Nov 27.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Tuesday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1 Tourism Asset	  3700.00   1.11</p>
<p> 2 Portman Min	     390.48   2.46</p>
<p> 3 Niugini Min	     236.69   3.29</p>
<p> 4 Mayne Nickless	  181.02   8.20</p>
<p> 5 TNT			 174.10   2.42</p>
<p> 6 Adel Bton Cement	121.74   1.68</p>
<p> 7 Colonial Coml	   120.22   2.20</p>
<p> 8 Forrestania Gold	 96.77   2.70</p>
<p> 9 Herald Rsc		 84.96   0.96</p>
<p>10 Westral Forest	   83.70   2.31</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1 Dominion Min		1.75   0.76</p>
<p> 2 Computer Power	    3.81   3.90</p>
<p> 3 Premier Inv		 4.17   0.74</p>
<p> 4 BTR Plc		     5.59   5.20</p>
<p> 5 Queensland Cotton	 5.67   4.30</p>
<p> 6 Parbury Ltd		 6.17   0.73</p>
<p> 7 Aust Gold Rsc	     6.96   1.27</p>
<p> 8 OLS Asia Hldgs	    7.56   0.90</p>
<p> 9 RGC			   7.67   5.29</p>
<p>10 Templeton Global	  7.94   1.39</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
